</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The above procedure for generating a constraint is adapted for each possible type of constraint.
Constraint consistency and subsumption, e.g., is defined differently for each constraint type.
As an example, Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> outlines the procedure for constructing an <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Always}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝗅𝗐𝖺𝗒𝗌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Always}</annotation></semantics></math> constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
We start by sampling a Boolean operation <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it op" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑜𝑝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it op</annotation></semantics></math> and a number of literals <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l\_no" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑛𝑜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l\_no</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, taking into account the parameters that are optionally provided by the user (see line <a href="#alg1.l3" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> of Algorihtm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Subsequently, we generate <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l\_no" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑛𝑜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l\_no</annotation></semantics></math> literals that are suitable for inclusion in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi</annotation></semantics></math> (lines <a href="#alg1.l4" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>–<a href="#alg1.l9" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).
We sample a literal <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> based on the atoms of the problem <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it F</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l5" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>), and then evaluate a set of conditions such that, if <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies one of them, then including <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is not meaningful with respect to constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For instance, it is not meaningful to include <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> if (i) <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> implies the goal <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it G</annotation></semantics></math>, as, in non-trivial problems where <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it I\not\models G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊧̸</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it I\not\models G</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l\rightarrow G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l\rightarrow G</annotation></semantics></math> implies that <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> does not hold in the initial state <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it I</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus cannot “always” hold; (ii) <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it G</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\neg l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\neg l</annotation></semantics></math>, because then <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> cannot hold in the final state of a plan that brings about <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it G</annotation></semantics></math>; (iii) if <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> does not hold in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it I</annotation></semantics></math>; or (iv) if <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied in every state in the sequence <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> induced by executing plan <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, as, in that case, <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(l)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(l)</annotation></semantics></math> is satisfied by optimal plan <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of the unconstrained problem, and thus adding <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> may not lead to a more complicated problem.
If any of the above conditions holds, then we drop <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> and sample another literal for our constraint (line <a href="#alg1.l6" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
Additionally, we resort to resampling if <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> has already been added to <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q</annotation></semantics></math> in a previous step, or the selected operation <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it op" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑜𝑝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it op</annotation></semantics></math> is a conjunction and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> is inconsistent with some other literal <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q</annotation></semantics></math>, taking into account a (possibly empty) set of atemporal domain axioms (see lines <a href="#alg1.l7" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>–<a href="#alg1.l8" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).
If none of the above conditions is satisfied, then we add <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l</annotation></semantics></math> to the set of literals that will be used to construct <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l9" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">After identifying <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it l\_no" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑛𝑜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it l\_no</annotation></semantics></math> literals that are suitable for constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>, we construct <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> using the sampled operation <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it op" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑜𝑝</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it op</annotation></semantics></math> (see lines <a href="#alg1.l10" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>–<a href="#alg1.l11" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> of Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Next, we need to verify whether <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is inconsistent or redundant with respect to the constraints that are already present in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it C</annotation></semantics></math>.
To do this, for each constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it C</annotation></semantics></math>, we check if <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is compatible with <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (lines <a href="#alg1.l12" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>–<a href="#alg1.l19" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>).
If <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is not compatible with some constraint in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it C</annotation></semantics></math>, then we drop <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> and generate another constraint.
Otherwise, if <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is compatible with every constraint in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it C</annotation></semantics></math>, then we add it in <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it C</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg1.l20" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Constrained Planning Problem Generator ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>).
For example, <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q{=}\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q{=}\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> is compatible with a <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Sometime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗈𝗆𝖾𝗍𝗂𝗆𝖾</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Sometime}</annotation></semantics></math> constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it q^{\prime}{=}\mathsf{S}(\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it q^{\prime}{=}\mathsf{S}(\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> if, according to the atemporal domain axioms, (i) <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi</annotation></semantics></math> does not imply <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi\rightarrow\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi\rightarrow\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> would imply that constraint <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{S}(\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{S}(\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is redundant given <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>; and (ii) <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> are consistent, because if they were inconsistent, it would be impossible to satisfy <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{A}(\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> given that <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{S}(\phi^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖲</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{S}(\phi^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> holds, i.e., in the case where <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\phi^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\phi^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is true in at least one state of a valid plan.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Automated LLM Plan Verifier</h3>

<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> LLM Plan Verifier</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            LLM plan <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math>, compiled problem <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math>, optimal cost <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Plan validation outcome: <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Invalid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗏𝖺𝗅𝗂𝖽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Invalid}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Suboptimal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗎𝖻𝗈𝗉𝗍𝗂𝗆𝖺𝗅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Suboptimal}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Optimal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖮𝗉𝗍𝗂𝗆𝖺𝗅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Optimal}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s\leftarrow I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s\leftarrow I</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a_{NL}\in\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a_{NL}\in\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it pddl\_format(a_{NL})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑝𝑑𝑑𝑙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑓𝑜𝑟𝑚𝑎𝑡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it pddl\_format(a_{NL})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a\leftarrow extract\_action(a_{NL})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝑒𝑥𝑡𝑟𝑎𝑐𝑡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a\leftarrow extract\_action(a_{NL})</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a\leftarrow closest\_action\_edit\_distance(a_{NL},\Pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝑐𝑙𝑜𝑠𝑒𝑠𝑡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑒𝑑𝑖𝑡</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑑𝑖𝑠𝑡𝑎𝑛𝑐𝑒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a\leftarrow closest\_action\_edit\_distance(a_{NL},\Pi)</annotation></semantics></math> 
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s\leftarrow simulate\_action(a,s,\Pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝑠𝑖𝑚𝑢𝑙𝑎𝑡𝑒</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑎𝑐𝑡𝑖𝑜𝑛</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s\leftarrow simulate\_action(a,s,\Pi)</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s{=}\mathsf{None}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗇𝖾</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s{=}\mathsf{None}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg2.l8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Invalid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗏𝖺𝗅𝗂𝖽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Invalid}</annotation></semantics></math> 
  
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s\not\models G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⊧̸</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s\not\models G</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg2.l9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Invalid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖨𝗇𝗏𝖺𝗅𝗂𝖽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Invalid}</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it length(\pi_{NL})&gt;c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑙𝑒𝑛𝑔𝑡ℎ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it length(\pi_{NL})&gt;c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> <span id="alg2.l10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Suboptimal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖲𝗎𝖻𝗈𝗉𝗍𝗂𝗆𝖺𝗅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Suboptimal}</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathsf{Optimal}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖮𝗉𝗍𝗂𝗆𝖺𝗅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathsf{Optimal}</annotation></semantics></math> 

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> outlines <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LexiCon</span>’s automated LLM plan verifier.
Its input is an LLM-generated plan <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math>, a PDDL problem <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> that has been compiled with <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\mathtt{LiftedTCORE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙻𝚒𝚏𝚝𝚎𝚍𝚃𝙲𝙾𝚁𝙴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\mathtt{LiftedTCORE}</annotation></semantics></math> and the optimal cost <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> that was discovered by <span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LexiCon</span> during constrained problem generation.
(Recall that a plan that is valid for the compiled version of a problem satisfies all the constraints in the original problem.)
Given this input, Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports whether <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is an invalid plan, a valid but suboptimal plan, or a valid, optimal plan for problem <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This is achieved in two steps: (i) simulating plan <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> to verify its validity, and, if <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is valid, (ii) comparing the length of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> to the optimal cost <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> in order to check whether <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To initiate the simulation of plan <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> over problem <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set variable <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math>, tracking the state of the problem, to the initial state <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it I</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg2.l3" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> of Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), and iterate over the actions in <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math>, in order to sequentially simulate the effects of each one over <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg2.l4" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
The prompt we use for LLM plan generation requests a specific format for LLM actions, so that they can be mapped directly to domain actiin in PDDL (line <a href="#alg2.l5" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
In practice, however, LLM actions may deviate from this format; we handle such cases by mapping the LLM-generated action <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> to the PDDL domain action yielding the shortest edit distance from <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> (line <a href="#alg2.l6" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
Both cases map <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> to a PDDL domain action <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a</annotation></semantics></math>, which we apply on the current state <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math> of our plan simulation (line <a href="#alg2.l7" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).
If the application of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a</annotation></semantics></math> does not lead to a new state, then we deduce that either the preconditions of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a</annotation></semantics></math> are not met in state <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math>, or that the application of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it a</annotation></semantics></math> over state <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math> led to the violation of a constraint of the original problem.
Thus, in this case, we deduce that plan <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is invalid.
If the simulation of all LLM-generated actions over <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math> succeeds, then we check whether the goal of the problem is satisfied in the final state <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math> reached in the simulation.
If the goal is not satisfied in <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math>, then plan <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is invalid (line <a href="#alg2.l9" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).
Otherwise, if the goal is satisfied in <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it s</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is valid, and we proceed with checking whether <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal or not.
If the length of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., the optimal cost of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\Pi^{cm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Π</mi><mi>𝑐𝑚</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\Pi^{cm}</annotation></semantics></math>, then plan <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is suboptimal (line <a href="#alg2.l10" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).
Otherwise, the length of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it c^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>c</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it c^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\it\pi_{NL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>𝑁𝐿</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\it\pi_{NL}</annotation></semantics></math> is an optimal plan for the problem (line <a href="#alg2.l11" title="In Algorithm 2 ‣ A.3 Automated LLM Plan Verifier ‣ Appendix A Reasoning Engine ‣ LexiCon: a Benchmark for Planningunder Temporal Constraints in Natural Language" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
